 ```
 
+#### Audio to video
+
+Pass a soundtrack with `--ref-audio` (the `ref_audios` video option) to
+generate the picture to it, e.g. a singer whose lips follow a song. The track
+is encoded with the audio VAE's encoder and held fixed (denoise mask 0, audio
+timestep 0) in the joint latent, so the output's soundtrack is the reference
+as the audio VAE reconstructs it. It combines with `--init-img` and
+`--end-img`, and with a latent upscale refine. The track must be at least as
+long as the video; the part after the video's length is ignored. It needs an
+audio VAE with encoder weights (`audio_vae.encoder.*`), as in
+`ltx-2.5-audio-vae-bf16.safetensors`.
+
+```sh
+./bin/sd-cli \
+  -M vid_gen \
+  --diffusion-model ../models/diffusion_models/ltx-2.5-22b-dev-transformer-Q8_0.gguf \
+  --vae ../models/vae/ltx-2.5-video-vae-conv-bf16.safetensors \
+  --audio-vae ../models/vae/ltx-2.5-audio-vae-bf16.safetensors \
+  --llm ../models/text_encoders/gemma4-12b-with-proj-ltx-2.5-Q8_0.gguf \
+  -p "close-up of a singer at a vintage microphone, singing. Audio: a man singing" \
+  -i ../inputs/singer.png \
+  --ref-audio ../inputs/song-section.wav \
+  --cfg-scale 3.0 \
+  --sampling-method euler \
+  -W 768 \
+  -H 512 \
+  --video-frames 97 \
+  --offload-to-cpu \
+  -v \
+  -o a2v.webm
+```
+
